{"term":"allow","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:97cad366375c3a47b7","definition":"To let one have as a suitable share of something.","example":"to allow a servant his liberty; to allow a free passage; to allow one day for rest","pos":"verb","synonyms":["grant","admit","afford","yield","give","permit","allot","bestow","concede"],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"ditransitive","register":"ditransitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:85f2014b4e33bcb955","definition":"To present something as possible or reasonable.","example":"The event allows of only one interpretation.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:51f33cf2a5204320b3","definition":"To permit, to give permission to.","example":"I will allow my son to be absent.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["permit","let","grant licence to","consent","grant"],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"catenative","register":"catenative, transitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:92d0f51073e1463f59","definition":"To not bar or obstruct.","example":"Although I don't consent to their holding such meetings, I will allow them for the time being.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["tolerate","suffer","permit","admit","concede"],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4634a3c71368d660b0","definition":"To acknowledge, accept the truth of; to concede; to accede to an opinion; to say something one agrees on in the context of a larger disagreement or reluctance.","example":"to allow a right; to allow a claim; to allow an appeal","pos":"verb","synonyms":["concede","accede","acquiesce"],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1df80d7fbfef79d604","definition":"To grant (something) as a deduction or an addition; especially to abate or deduct.","example":"to allow a sum for leakage","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:458f66405161ca2ffa","definition":"To make an allowance, to take into account when making plans.","example":"When calculating a budget for a construction project, always allow for contingencies.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8dd37cdf45fb1c6801","definition":"To render physically possible.","example":"The inlet allowed a facility to bring the money in a boat secretly and at night to the very foot of the hill.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bc0387c7755136cb2b","definition":"To praise; to approve of; hence, to sanction.","example":"Truly ye bear witness that ye allow the deeds of your fathers","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f9a4ea003552955f1f","definition":"To sanction; to invest; to entrust.","example":"Therefore so please thee to return with us,\nAnd of our Athens—thine and ours—to take\nThe captainship, thou shalt be met with thanks,\nAllow'd with absolute power, and thy good name\nLive with authority. So soon we shall drive back\nOf Alcibiades the approaches wild,\nWho, like a boar too savage, doth root up\nHis country's peace.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c892192ebcc7f6fc03","definition":"To like; to be suited or pleased with.","example":"How allow you the model of these clothes?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e2a7137272fa2c1444","definition":"To decide (a request) in favour of the party who raised it; to grant victory to a party regarding (a request).","example":"to allow an objection","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:55c7307b5955101854","definition":"To forgo bothering with, to let slide.","example":"Easy on violence, now I doubt it\nI could’ve banged this face but allowed it","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["ban","forbid","prohibit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"Multicultural-London-English","register":"Multicultural-London-English, transitive","wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/əˈlaʊ/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/6d/En-us-allow.ogg/En-us-allow.ogg.mp3","uk":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/68/En-uk-to_allow.ogg/En-uk-to_allow.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["allowability","allowable","allowance","allowee","allower","allow for","allowingly","allow it","allowment","allow nature to take her","its course","disallowance","reallow","unallowing"]}